    <!-- TAB I: THE QUESTION — editorial framing essay -->
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <div class="tab-content active" id="tab-question">

        <div class="section-intro">
            <h2>How can the Power Law channel itself become a <em>discipline?</em></h2>
            <p>The Power Law page makes a structural argument: bitcoin's price oscillates inside a bounded channel, with a conservative floor at 0.42&times; trend, a central trend, and an upper boundary at 3&times; trend that historical excursions briefly touch. Across fifteen years and nine orders of magnitude, that channel has held with R&sup2; above 0.95. Most readers encounter this as a model to believe or reject.</p>
            <p>There is another reading. The channel can be treated not as a forecast but as a <em>protocol</em>. If price oscillates between bounds, then bounded triggers &mdash; sell when the historical distribution says you're in a high-percentile zone, rebuy when it says you're in a low-percentile zone &mdash; transform the model from a thing-you-believe-in into a thing-you-act-on. The channel becomes a discipline.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- ═══════════════════ CHANNEL ORIENTATION CHART ═══════════════════ -->
        <!-- Simplified version of the Calculator-tab chart: just floor, trend, -->
        <!-- upper bound, and historical price. Strips out the user's threshold -->
        <!-- lines and trigger markers — those belong in the Calculator. This  -->
        <!-- chart's job is to make 'channel', 'floor', 'trend', 'upper bound'  -->
        <!-- concrete before the essay's structural argument unfolds below.   -->
        <div class="dr-q-channel-viz">
            <div class="dr-q-channel-title">The Power Law channel &mdash; fifteen years of bitcoin price against floor, trend, and upper bound, projected forward</div>
            <div class="dr-q-channel-chart-wrapper" data-chart-copy data-chart-heading="closest:.dr-q-channel-viz .dr-q-channel-title" data-chart-title="The Power Law channel"><canvas id="drQuestionChannelChart"></canvas></div>
            <div class="dr-q-channel-legend">
